t.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/debruijn_code_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_benchmark_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_contract_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/debruijn_vm_contract_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/linearize_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/macro_build_test.clj\n M test/yin/vm/macro_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/parity_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_engine_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_ffi_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_stream_observer_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/telemetry_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/ucf_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm_test.cljc\n?? test/yin/vm/rule_r_test.cljc\n?? test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj\n     1\t(ns yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\n     2\t  \"The store-write audit (Rule R, the store-key invariant): every program\n     3\t   store write goes through `yin.vm.engine/store-put`, which refuses a\n     4\t   reserved key; every other store mutation it detects is state\n     5\t   construction on an allowlist. This gate reads every source file under\n     6\t   `src` as forms (tools.reader, reader conditionals preserved, so every\n     7\t   host's branch is read) and fails on any detected site outside the\n     8\t   allowlist, on any allowlisted site that no longer exists, and on any\n     9\t   source file it cannot read. The allowlist is exact for what the\n    10\t   detector sees; what it sees is exactly this:\n    11\t\n    12\t   - A call whose head is one of `mutation-heads` and that touches a store:\n    13\t     a `:store` argument (`(assoc vm :store x)`, `(update vm :store ...)`),\n    14\t     a key path whose first key is `:store` or that contains it\n    15\t     (`(assoc-in vm [:store k] v)`), or a store as its target. A store is a\n    16\t     symbol named `store`, `new-store`, `store0`, ...; `(:store x)`,\n    17\t     `(get x :store)`, or `(get-in x [:store ...])`; or a local alias of\n    18\t     one of these.\n    19\t   - A local alias: a symbol bound to a store by `let`, `let*`, `loop`,\n    20\t     `loop*`, `when-let`, `if-let`, `when-some`, `if-some`, or\n    21\t     `binding`, directly or through an earlier alias in the same or an\n    22\t     enclosing binding form, and a map destructuring key bound to `:store`\n    23\t     (`{heap :store}`). The alias is scoped to the binding form's body.\n    24\t   - A pipeline whose threaded value is a store: `->`, `->>`, `some->`,\n    25\t     `some->>`, `cond->`, `cond->>` (forms only, tests skipped), and\n    26\t     `doto`. The value is a store from the start when the pipeline's\n    27\t     initial value is a store (a store symbol, `(:store x)`,\n    28\t     `(get x :store)`, `(get-in x [:store ...])`, or a scoped alias), or\n    29\t     from the first step that moves onto one (`:store`, `(:store)`,\n    30\t     `(get :store)`, `(get-in [:store ...])`). Every mutation-head step\n    31\t     from then on is a site. This is conservative: a later step that leaves\n    32\t     the store (`(get 'k)`) does not end it.\n    33\t   - `as->`: its name is a store alias from the start when the initial\n    34\t     value is a store, and after any step that is one.\n    35\t   - A mutation step of any pipeline whose own arguments touch a store\n    36\t     (`(->> v (assoc (:store vm) k))`), found by the ordinary walk.\n    37\t   - Every `store-put` call, and every map literal with a `:store` key (a\n    38\t     map rebuilt around the store).\n    39\t\n    40\t   A site is identified by its file, the name of its top-level form, and\n    41\t   its head, with a count, so the allowlist does not move with line\n    42\t   numbers. `negative-fixtures` pins every covered form above, each\n    43\t   pipeline shape both seeded with an extracted store and with a\n    44\t   let-bound alias.\n    45\t\n    46\t   Residual, NOT detected, pinned by `residual-fixtures`: a store passed\n    47\t   across a function boundary and written under the parameter's own name\n    48\t   (`(defn g [heap v] (assoc heap k v))` called as `(g (:store vm) v)`),\n    49\t   a store carried inside another data structure (a map, an atom, a\n    50\t   collection taken apart by `when-first`) and written from there, and a\n    51\t   mutation built dynamically (`apply`, `partial`, `comp`, a head bound\n    52\t   to another name). Also outside the detector, with no fixture:\n    53\t   transients, host interop, and macros that expand to a write. Those\n    54\t   need review; this gate does not prove them absent. JVM only: it reads\n    55\t   source files.\"\n    56\t  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    57\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    58\t            [clojure.tools.reader :as reader]\n    59\t            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(declare walk-sites)\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(def ^:private mutation-heads\n    66\t  #{\"assoc\" \"assoc-in\" \"update\" \"update-in\" \"merge\" \"merge-with\" \"into\"\n    67\t    \"dissoc\" \"select-keys\" \"conj\" \"swap!\" \"reset!\" \"vswap!\" \"vreset!\"\n    68\t    \"store-put\"})\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(def ^:private binding-heads\n    72\t  #{\"let\" \"let*\" \"loop\" \"loop*\" \"when-let\" \"if-let\" \"when-some\" \"if-some\"\n    73\t    \"binding\"})\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t(def ^:private threading-heads\n    77\t  \"Pipelines whose steps receive the threaded value: `doto` receives the\n    78\t   initial value at every step.\"\n    79\t  #{\"->\" \"->>\" \"some->\" \"some->>\" \"doto\"})\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(def ^:private conditional-threading-heads\n    83\t  \"Pipelines whose steps alternate test and form.\"\n    84\t  #{\"cond->\" \"cond->>\"})\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\t(defn- store-symbol?\n    88\t  [x]\n    89\t  (and (symbol? x)\n    90\t       (boolean (re-find #\"(^|-)store\\d*'?$\" (name x)))))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(defn- store-read?\n    94\t  \"`(:store x)`, `(get x :store)`, or `(get-in x [:store ...])`.\"\n    95\t  [x]\n    96\t  (and (seq? x)\n    97\t       (or (= :store (first x))\n    98\t           (and (= 'get (first x)) (= :store (nth x 2 nil)))\n    99\t           (and (= 'get-in (first x))\n   100\t                (vector? (nth x 2 nil))\n   101\t                (= :store (first (nth x 2)))))))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn- store-expr?\n   105\t  [x aliases]\n   106\t  (or (store-symbol? x) (contains? aliases x) (store-read? x)))\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t(defn- head-name\n   110\t  [form]\n   111\t  (when (and (seq? form) (symbol? (first form)))\n   112\t    (name (first form))))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn- mutation?\n   116\t  [form aliases]\n   117\t  (let [[head & args] form]\n   118\t    (and (contains? mutation-heads (head-name form))\n   119\t         (or (= \"store-put\" (name head))\n   120\t             (some #(= :store %) args)\n   121\t             (some #(and (vector? %) (some #{:store} %)) args)\n   122\t             (store-expr? (first args) aliases)))))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn- bound-aliases\n   126\t  \"The symbols `lhs` binds to a store, given its `init`.\"\n   127\t  [lhs init aliases]\n   128\t  (cond (symbol? lhs) (if (store-expr? init aliases) #{lhs} #{})\n   129\t        (map? lhs) (into #{}\n   130\t                         (keep (fn [[k v]]\n   131\t                                 (when (and (symbol? k) (= :store v)) k)))\n   132\t                         lhs)\n   133\t        :else #{}))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn- through-store?\n   137\t  \"A pipeline step that moves the threaded value onto a store: `:store`,\n   138\t   `(:store)`, `(get :store)`, or `(get-in [:store ...])`.\"\n   139\t  [step]\n   140\t  (or (= :store step)\n   141\t      (and (seq? step) (= :store (first step)))\n   142\t      (and (seq? step) (= 'get (first step)) (= :store (second step)))\n   143\t      (and (seq? step) (= 'get-in (first step))\n   144\t           (vector? (second step)) (= :store (first (second step))))))\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\t(defn- mutation-step\n   148\t  \"The head string of a mutation-head step, or nil.\"\n   149\t  [step]\n   150\t  (cond (and (seq? step) (contains? mutation-heads (head-name step)))\n   151\t        (str (first step))\n   152\t        (and (symbol? step) (contains? mutation-heads (name step)))\n   153\t        (str step)))\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\t(defn- threaded-sites\n   157\t  \"Mutation-head steps of a pipeline once its threaded value is a store:\n   158\t   from the start when the initial value is a store (`store-expr?`, a\n   159\t   scoped alias included), or from the first step that moves onto one\n   160\t   (`through-store?`). Conservative: a later step that leaves the store\n   161\t   does not end it. `cond->`/`cond->>` steps are their forms, skipping\n   162\t   the tests.\"\n   163\t  [form aliases]\n   164\t  (let [h (head-name form)\n   165\t        [_ init & more] (when (seq? form) form)\n   166\t        steps (cond (contains? threading-heads h) more\n   167\t                    (contains? conditional-threading-heads h)\n   168\t                    (take-nth 2 (rest more))\n   169\t                    :else nil)]\n   170\t    (when (some? steps)\n   171\t      (loop [store? (store-expr? init aliases)\n   172\t             steps steps\n   173\t             acc []]\n   174\t        (if-let [[step & more] (seq steps)]\n   175\t          (recur (or store? (through-store? step))\n   176\t                 more\n   177\t                 (if-let [site (when store? (mutation-step step))]\n   178\t                   (conj acc site)\n   179\t                   acc))\n   180\t          acc)))))\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\t(defn- as->-sites\n   184\t  \"`(as-> init name & steps)`: `name` is a store alias from the start when\n   185\t   `init` is a store, and from the step after any step that is one.\"\n   186\t  [form aliases]\n   187\t  (let [[_ init nm & steps] form]\n   188\t    (loop [store? (store-expr? init aliases)\n   189\t           steps steps\n   190\t           acc (vec (walk-sites init aliases))]\n   191\t      (if-let [[step & more] (seq steps)]\n   192\t        (let [al (if store? (conj aliases nm) aliases)]\n   193\t          (recur (or store? (store-expr? step al))\n   194\t                 more\n   195\t                 (into acc (walk-sites step al))))\n   196\t        acc))))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t(defn- walk-sites\n   200\t  \"Every site inside `form` under the store `aliases` in scope: a head\n   201\t   string for a mutation, `:map` for a map literal with a `:store` key.\"\n   202\t  [form aliases]\n   203\t  (cond\n   204\t    (reader-conditional? form) (walk-sites (:form form) aliases)\n   205\t    (and (= \"as->\" (head-name form)) (symbol? (nth form 2 nil)))\n   206\t    (as->-sites form aliases)\n   207\t    (and (contains? binding-heads (head-name form))\n   208\t         (vector? (second form)))\n   209\t    (let [[_ bindings & body] form\n   210\t          [sites inner] (reduce (fn [[sites al] [lhs init]]\n   211\t                                  [(into sites (walk-sites init al))\n   212\t                                   (into al (bound-aliases lhs init al))])\n   213\t                                [[] aliases]\n   214\t                                (partition 2 bindings))]\n   215\t      (into sites (mapcat #(walk-sites % inner)) body))\n   216\t    (seq? form)\n   217\t    (concat (when (mutation? form aliases) [(str (first form))])\n   218\t            (threaded-sites form aliases)\n   219\t            (mapcat #(walk-sites % aliases) form))\n   220\t    (map? form)\n   221\t    (concat (when (contains? form :store) [:map])\n   222\t            (mapcat #(walk-sites % aliases) (concat (keys form) (vals form))))\n   223\t    (coll? form) (mapcat #(walk-sites % aliases) form)\n   224\t    :else nil))\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\t(defn- form-sites\n   228\t  [form]\n   229\t  (walk-sites form #{}))\n   230\t\n   231\t\n   232\t(defn- top-level-name\n   233\t  [form]\n   234\t  (if (and (seq? form) (symbol? (second form)))\n   235\t    (str (second form))\n   236\t    (pr-str (if (seq? form) (first form) form))))\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\t(defn- alias-map\n   240\t  \"Every `:as alias` in the source, resolved to itself: enough for\n   241\t   tools.reader to read `::alias/kw` without loading the namespace.\"\n   242\t  [text]\n   243\t  (into {}\n   244\t        (map (fn [[_ a]] [(symbol a) (symbol a)]))\n   245\t        (re-seq #\":as\\s+([A-Za-z0-9.*+!_?<>=-]+)\" text)))\n   246\t\n   247\t\n   248\t(defn sites-in-source\n   249\t  \"`{[top-level-name head] count}` of the store mutations in `text`, or\n   250\t   `{[:unreadable] 1}` when the text cannot be read as forms.\"\n   251\t  [text]\n   252\t  (try\n   253\t    (binding [reader/*alias-map* (alias-map text)\n   254\t              reader/*default-data-reader-fn* (fn [_ v] v)\n   255\t              *ns* (create-ns 'yin.vm.store-write-audit-reader)]\n   256\t      (let [rdr (rt/indexing-push-back-reader text)\n   257\t            opts {:read-cond :preserve, :eof ::eof}]\n   258\t        (loop [acc {}]\n   259\t          (let [form (reader/read opts rdr)]\n   260\t            (if (= ::eof form)\n   261\t              acc\n   262\t              (recur (reduce (fn [acc head]\n   263\t                               (update acc [(top-level-name form) head]\n   264\t                                       (fnil inc 0)))\n   265\t                             acc\n   266\t                             (form-sites form))))))))\n   267\t    (catch Exception e\n   268\t      {[:unreadable (ex-message e)] 1})))\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\t(defn- source-files\n   272\t  []\n   273\t  (->> (file-seq (io/file \"src\"))\n   274\t       (filter #(.isFile ^java.io.File %))\n   275\t       (map #(.getPath ^java.io.File %))\n   276\t       (filter #(re-find #\"\\.clj[csd]?$\" %))\n   277\t       sort))\n   278\t\n   279\t\n   280\t(defn source-sites\n   281\t  \"file -> `{[top-level-name head] count}` for every file with a site.\"\n   282\t  []\n   283\t  (into {}\n   284\t        (keep (fn [f]\n   285\t                (let [sites (sites-in-source (slurp f))]\n   286\t                  (when (seq sites) [f sites]))))\n   287\t        (source-files)))\n   288\t\n   289\t\n   290\t(def allowlist\n   291\t  \"file -> {[top-level-name head] count}, with the reason each may write.\"\n   292\t  {\"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\"\n   293\t   {;; the one program write, and the :vm/store-put effect dispatcher\n   294\t    [\"store-put\" \"assoc\"] 1\n   295\t    [\"handle-effect\" \"store-put\"] 1\n   296\t    [\"handle-effect\" \"assoc\"] 1\n   297\t    ;; engine-minted keyword keys: stream ids, cursor ids, cursor advance\n   298\t    [\"handle-make\" \"assoc\"] 2\n   299\t    [\"handle-cursor\" \"assoc\"] 2\n   300\t    [\"handle-next\" \"assoc\"] 2\n   301\t    [\"waitset-resolver\" \"assoc\"] 1\n   302\t    [\"check-wait-set\" \"assoc\"] 1\n   303\t    ;; the ready-queue merge, asserted to carry only keyword keys\n   304\t    [\"resume-from-run-queue\" \"assoc\"] 1\n   305\t    [\"resume-from-run-queue\" \"merge\"] 1}\n   306\t   ;; program writes through engine/store-put: the definition transition,\n   307\t   ;; :vm/store-put, and :vm/store-update\n   308\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc\"\n   309\t   {[\"cesk-transition\" \"assoc\"] 3\n   310\t    [\"cesk-transition\" \"engine/store-put\"] 3}\n   311\t   ;; opcodes 11 (store-put) and 24 (define), through engine/store-put\n   312\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc\"\n   313\t   {[\"vm-hot\" \"assoc\"] 2\n   314\t    [\"vm-hot\" \"engine/store-put\"] 2}\n   315\t   ;; the constructor merge (checked) and :store-put/:define through\n   316\t   ;; engine/store-put\n   317\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc\"\n   318\t   {[\"create-vm\" :map] 1\n   319\t    [\"create-vm\" \"merge\"] 1\n   320\t    [\"step1\" \"assoc\"] 2\n   321\t    [\"step1\" \"engine/store-put\"] 2}\n   322\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc\"\n   323\t   {[\"create-vm\" :map] 1\n   324\t    [\"create-vm\" \"merge\"] 1\n   325\t    [\"step1\" \"assoc\"] 2\n   326\t    [\"step1\" \"engine/store-put\"] 2}\n   327\t   ;; construction: the FFI pair under minted keyword keys\n   328\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\"\n   329\t   {[\"empty-state\" :map] 1}\n   330\t   ;; dao.await: minted keyword keys, checked\n   331\t   \"src/cljc/dao/await.cljc\"\n   332\t   {[\"run\" \"update\"] 1}\n   333\t   ;; the waitset library's result carries the store its :advance wrote\n   334\t   \"src/cljc/dao/stream/waitset.cljc\"\n   335\t   {[\"check\" :map] 1}\n   336\t   ;; a dao.space published-index handle, not a VM store\n   337\t   \"src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc\"\n   338\t   {[\"open-published!\" :map] 1}\n   339\t   ;; the REPL history keys *1 *2 *3 (fixed symbols, none reserved), and\n   340\t   ;; the expander consumer's macro store\n   341\t   \"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"\n   342\t   {[\"inject-last-value\" \"update\"] 1\n   343\t    [\"make-expander\" :map] 1}\n   344\t   ;; the handoff demo: shipped definitions, checked\n   345\t   \"src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc\"\n   346\t   {[\"datoms->semantic-vm\" \"update\"] 1}\n   347\t   ;; a JVM demo moving one VM's whole store to another\n   348\t   \"src/clj/yin/demo.clj\"\n   349\t   {[\"run-demo\" \"assoc\"] 1}\n   350\t   ;; display projections of a VM's store in the browser demos\n   351\t   \"src/cljs/datomworld/demo/compilation_pipeline.cljs\"\n   352\t   {[\"walker-cesk\" :map] 1}\n   353\t   \"src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs\"\n   354\t   {[\"vm->cesk\" :map] 1}\n   355\t   ;; the expander's macro store: harvest refuses the reserved key,\n   356\t   ;; post-harvest installs only harvested names, make-ctx refuses a\n   357\t   ;; seeded store binding it, expand-batch threads the checked store\n   358\t   \"src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\"\n   359\t   {[\"harvest\" \"assoc\"] 1\n   360\t    [\"harvest\" \"dissoc\"] 1\n   361\t    [\"post-harvest\" \"assoc\"] 1\n   362\t    [\"post-harvest\" \"dissoc\"] 1\n   363\t    [\"make-ctx\" :map] 1\n   364\t    [\"expand-batch\" \"assoc\"] 2}})\n   365\t\n   366\t\n   367\t(deftest every-store-mutation-is-on-the-allowlist\n   368\t  (is (= allowlist (source-sites))\n   369\t      \"a new store mutation must go through engine/store-put or join the\n   370\t       allowlist with its reason; an unreadable file fails too\"))\n   371\t\n   372\t\n   373\t(def negative-fixtures\n   374\t  \"Common store-mutation forms outside the allowlist; each must be caught.\"\n   375\t  [\"(defn f [state v] (assoc-in state [:store 'yin/def] v))\"\n   376\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (update vm :store assoc 'x v))\"\n   377\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (update-in vm [:store 'x] (constantly v)))\"\n   378\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (assoc vm :store (conj (:store vm) ['x v])))\"\n   379\t   \"(defn f [vm] (dissoc (:store vm) 'x))\"\n   380\t   \"(defn f [vm ks] (select-keys (get vm :store) ks))\"\n   381\t   \"(defn f [store v] (into store {'x v}))\"\n   382\t   \"(defn f [new-store v]\\n  (merge\\n    new-store\\n    {'x v}))\"\n   383\t   \"(defn f [a v] (swap! a assoc-in [:store 'x] v))\"\n   384\t   \"(defn f [a v] (reset! a {:store v}))\"\n   385\t   \"(defn f [vm m] (merge-with merge vm {:store m}))\"\n   386\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (engine/store-put (:store vm) 'x v))\"\n   387\t   \"(defn f [vm v] #?(:clj (assoc-in vm [:store 'x] v) :cljs vm))\"\n   388\t   ;; local aliases of a store value\n   389\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [heap (:store vm)] (assoc heap 'yin/def v)))\"\n   390\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (get vm :store) h2 h] (assoc h2 'x v)))\"\n   391\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (get-in vm [:store])] (merge h {'x v})))\"\n   392\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (when-let [h (:store vm)] (conj h ['x v])))\"\n   393\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (if-let [h (:store vm)] (dissoc h 'x) vm))\"\n   394\t   \"(defn f [vm] (loop [h (:store vm)] (recur (assoc h 'x 1))))\"\n   395\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [{heap :store} vm] (assoc heap 'x v)))\"\n   396\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (let [g 1] (assoc h 'x g))))\"\n   397\t   ;; a pipeline threaded through the store\n   398\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (-> vm :store (assoc 'x v)))\"\n   399\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (some-> vm (get :store) (update 'x inc)))\"\n   400\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (->> vm :store (merge {'x v})))\"\n   401\t   ;; a pipeline seeded with an extracted store\n   402\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (-> (:store vm) (assoc 'yin/def v)))\"\n   403\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (->> (:store vm) (merge {'x v})))\"\n   404\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (some-> (get vm :store) (assoc 'x v)))\"\n   405\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (some->> (get-in vm [:store]) (merge {'x v})))\"\n   406\t   \"(defn f [store v] (-> store (dissoc 'x)))\"\n   407\t   ;; a pipeline seeded with a let-bound alias\n   408\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (-> h (assoc 'x v))))\"\n   409\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (->> h (merge {'x v}))))\"\n   410\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (some-> h (dissoc 'x))))\"\n   411\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (some->> h (merge {'x v}))))\"\n   412\t   ;; the other threading and seeding shapes\n   413\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (cond-> (:store vm) v (assoc 'x v)))\"\n   414\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (cond->> (:store vm) v (merge {'x v})))\"\n   415\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (cond-> vm v :store v (assoc 'x v)))\"\n   416\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (as-> (:store vm) s (assoc s 'x v)))\"\n   417\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (as-> vm m (:store m) (assoc m 'x v)))\"\n   418\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (as-> h s (conj s ['x v]))))\"\n   419\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (doto (:store vm) (assoc 'x v)))\"\n   420\t   ;; a store passed as the first argument of a threaded call\n   421\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (->> v (assoc (:store vm) 'x)))\"\n   422\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (-> 'x (as-> k (assoc h k v)))))\"\n   423\t   ;; every mutation head and store-symbol spelling the docstring names\n   424\t   \"(defn f [store v] (vswap! store assoc 'x v))\"\n   425\t   \"(defn f [store] (vreset! store {}))\"\n   426\t   \"(defn f [store0 v] (conj store0 ['x v]))\"\n   427\t   ;; every binding form the docstring names\n   428\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let* [h (:store vm)] (assoc h 'x v)))\"\n   429\t   \"(defn f [vm] (loop* [h (:store vm)] (recur (dissoc h 'x))))\"\n   430\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (when-some [h (:store vm)] (assoc h 'x v)))\"\n   431\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (if-some [h (:store vm)] (assoc h 'x v) vm))\"\n   432\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (binding [h (:store vm)] (assoc h 'x v)))\"\n   433\t   ;; every step that moves a pipeline onto the store\n   434\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (-> vm (:store) (assoc 'x v)))\"\n   435\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (-> vm (get-in [:store]) (dissoc 'x)))\"\n   436\t   ;; the remaining pipeline shapes seeded with a let-bound alias\n   437\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (cond-> h v (assoc 'x v))))\"\n   438\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (cond->> h v (merge {'x v}))))\"\n   439\t   \"(defn f [vm v] (let [h (:store vm)] (doto h (assoc 'x v))))\"])\n   440\t\n    40\t`:parked`, `:ready-queue`, and `:wait-set` looking for `:compiled-version`\n    41\tinside `:next`-chained frames. On a payload without those keys they find\n    42\tnothing, which is correct; no VM in this repository uses the compiled cache.\n    43\t\n    44\t### 1.1 Names and the program store (Rule R)\n    45\t\n    46\t`yin/def` is syntax, never a name. Two engine functions carry that rule\n    47\tfor every VM:\n    48\t\n    49\t    resolve-var      env store primitives registry name -> value\n    50\t    store-put        store key val -> store       (refuses a reserved key)\n    51\t\n    52\t`resolve-var` refuses a reserved name (`:reserved-name`, role\n    53\t`:variable`) before it consults env or store; every executing variable\n    54\tlookup of all four VMs goes through it. `store-put`, with its guard\n    55\t`check-store-key!`, is the one program store write: the `:vm/store-put`\n    56\teffect dispatcher, the direct store instructions of the walker, semantic,\n    57\tstack, and register VMs, and all four definition transitions write\n    58\tthrough it, and none of those transitions resolves its operator. A\n    59\tprogram therefore cannot redirect a definition through any binding.\n    60\t\n    61\t`resume-from-run-queue` asserts that a ready entry's `:store-updates`\n    62\tcarries only keyword keys, the ones the engine mints, and refuses any\n    63\tother key with `{:rule :store-update-key}`.\n    64\t\n    65\tEvery other store write the audit detects is state construction and\n    66\tsits on an allowlist, enforced by the store-write audit\n    67\t(`test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj`). The allowlist is exact for\n    68\twhat the detector sees, and no more. The audit reads every file under\n    69\t`src` as forms, every host's reader-conditional branch included, and\n    70\tdetects:\n    71\t\n    72\t- an `assoc`, `assoc-in`, `update`, `update-in`, `merge`, `merge-with`,\n    73\t  `into`, `dissoc`, `select-keys`, `conj`, `swap!`, `reset!`, `vswap!`,\n    74\t  or `vreset!` whose argument is `:store`, whose key path contains\n    75\t  `:store`, or whose target is a store: a symbol named `store`,\n    76\t  `new-store`, `store0`, ..., `(:store x)`, `(get x :store)`,\n    77\t  `(get-in x [:store ...])`, or a local alias of one;\n    78\t- a local alias bound by `let`, `let*`, `loop`, `loop*`, `when-let`,\n    79\t  `if-let`, `when-some`, `if-some`, or `binding`, directly or through an\n    80\t  earlier alias, or by a `{heap :store}` destructuring key, scoped to the\n    81\t  binding form's body;\n    82\t- a pipeline whose threaded value is a store: `->`, `->>`, `some->`,\n    83\t  `some->>`, `cond->` and `cond->>` (forms only), and `doto`. The value\n    84\t  is a store from the start when the initial value is a store (any of\n    85\t  the store forms above, a scoped alias included), or from the first step\n    86\t  that moves onto one (`:store`, `(:store)`, `(get :store)`,\n    87\t  `(get-in [:store ...])`); every mutation-head step from then on is a\n    88\t  site, conservatively, even after a step that leaves the store;\n    89\t- `as->`, whose name is a store alias from a store initial value, or\n    90\t  after any step that is a store;\n    91\t- every `store-put` call and every map literal with a `:store` key.\n    92\t\n    93\tIt fails on any detected site, keyed by file, top-level form, and head,\n    94\toutside the list, on any listed site that is gone, and on an unreadable\n    95\tfile. Negative fixtures pin every form above: each mutation head and\n    96\tstore spelling, each binding form, each pipeline shape seeded both with\n    97\tan extracted store and with a let-bound alias, and each step that moves\n    98\ta pipeline onto the store.\n    99\t\n   100\tIt does NOT detect, and review must cover: a store passed across a\n   101\tfunction boundary and written under the parameter's own name; a store\n   102\tcarried inside another data structure (a map, an atom, a collection\n   103\ttaken apart by `when-first`) and written from there; and a mutation\n   104\tbuilt dynamically (`apply`, `partial`, `comp`, a head bound to another\n   105\tname). Residual fixtures pin each of these as undetected, so the stated\n   106\tguarantee cannot silently drift from the code. Transients, host\n   107\tinterop, and macros that expand to a write are outside the detector too,\n   108\twith no fixture.\n   109\t\n   110\tThe list: program writes through `engine/store-put`; engine-minted\n   111\tkeyword keys (stream ids, cursor ids, and cursor advance in\n   112\t`handle-next` and the wait-set resolver); the ready-queue merge\n   113\t(asserted keyword keys); VM construction (the FFI pair, and the two de\n   114\tBruijn constructor merges, checked); `dao.await` (checked keyword\n   115\tkeys); the REPL history keys `*1`, `*2`, `*3`; the continuation handoff\n   116\tdemo (checked); a JVM demo store transfer (`src/clj/yin/demo.clj`);\n   117\tdisplay projections in two browser demos; the waitset result and a\n   118\tdao.space index handle, which are not VM program writes; and the\n   119\texpander's macro store. A new store write must either route through\n   120\t`store-put` or join the allowlist in review.\n   121\t\n   122\t## 2. What a VM supplies\n   123\t\n   124\tExactly one VM-level function and one instruction-site builder shape.\n   125\t\n   126\t### 2.1 The restore function\n   127\t\n   128\t    restore : base entry val -> state\n   129\t\n   130\t`base` is the VM state after the engine has done its part: the ready entry\n   448\tRe-entry after invocation increments depth. Re-check after an operator rewrite\n   449\tdoes not, because recognition is not expansion. A generated chain therefore\n   450\tconsumes depth and cannot rewrite forever at a constant value.\n   451\t\n   452\t`invoke` runs the transformer on the bounded runner (S5.2), which is a\n   453\twalker: it inherits the walker's Rule R transition checks, so a\n   454\ttransformer body that reads, binds, or stores under `yin/def` is refused\n   455\twhen it runs. `invoke` verifies the entry's contract before anything\n   456\truns, direct calls included, and hands that verified stamp to the\n   457\trunner in its request (`:contract`); the runner checks it again and\n   458\tloads the body rows under it, never under a stamp of its own. The\n   459\texpander's input batches themselves carry no stamp: they are syntax\n   460\tadmitted by `valid-tree?`, and the packets harvested from them are this\n   461\texpander's fresh output.\n   462\t\n   463\t**Limitation (deferred, not closed by Rule R commit one).** Harvest\n   464\tstamps the packets it produces with the current AST contract, and that\n   465\tis sound only if every input batch is fresh source syntax, as this\n   466\tspecification assumes of `program-in`. The expander's API cannot\n   467\testablish that provenance: nothing distinguishes a batch a frontend just\n   468\tproduced from one replayed out of storage, so a persisted batch admitted\n   469\there would have its macro bodies stamped current. Admitting persisted\n   470\tbatches as code needs a stamped-input design, which is not specified\n   471\there; until then a composition must feed the expander fresh syntax only.\n   472\t\n   473\t### 4.3 Properties\n   474\t\n   475\t- **Outermost first:** a transformer sees operands as written.\n   476\t- **Fixpoint:** each returned tree is reconsidered, including applications\n   477\t  whose operator becomes a macro name.\n   478\t- **Lexical shadowing:** lambda parameters shadow macro names only in their\n   479\t  body, never in sibling operands of the lambda's application occurrence.\n   480\t- **Occurrence correctness:** paths distinguish one shared row under different\n   481\t  lexical ancestors.\n   482\t- **Determinism:** grammar order, operand order, harvest ordinal, and explicit\n   483\t  attempt state are the only orders used.\n   484\t- **Failure record:** the event begins before guards and invocation, so every\n   485\t  recognized call records success or error.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
