mplements all 23 opcodes, Rule R's `:define` included,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:156:   `contract` is required and compared with `vm/register-contract` first\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:162:    (vm/check-contract! vm/register-contract contract))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:415:      (let [val (engine/resolve-var free-env store primitives modules\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:510:               :store (engine/store-put store key val)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:512:      ;; :define -- the definition transition: register `rs` is written\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:515:      :define\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:520:               :store (engine/store-put store (nth inst 2) val)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:11:   `[:ffi-call op argc]`, `[:define name]` (Rule R's definition\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:65:;; `yin.vm.engine/resolve-var` implements for the named VM. :hash is the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:121:   `contract` is required and compared with `vm/stack-contract` first\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:127:    (vm/check-contract! vm/stack-contract contract)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:409:            value (engine/resolve-var free-env store primitives modules\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:507:               :store (engine/store-put store key value)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:509:      ;; :define -- the definition transition: pop the value, write it\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:512:      :define\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:517:               :store (engine/store-put store (nth inst 1) value)))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn resolve-var\n    55\t  \"Look up a variable name: env -> store -> primitives -> module registry.\n    56\t\n    57\t   A reserved name (Rule R: `yin/def` is syntax, never a name) is refused\n    58\t   before env or store is consulted, so no binding, store entry, or\n    59\t   registry can give it a meaning. Every executing variable lookup of\n    60\t   every engine goes through here.\n    61\t\n    62\t   The registry is a value supplied by the composition, not a global.\"\n    63\t  [env store primitives registry name]\n    64\t  (when (vm/reserved-name? name)\n    65\t    (vm/refuse-reserved! :variable name))\n    66\t  (if-let [pair (find env name)]\n    67\t    (val pair)\n    68\t    (if-let [pair (find store name)]\n    69\t      (val pair)\n    70\t      (if-let [pair (find primitives name)]\n    71\t        (vm/primitive-function (val pair))\n    72\t        (if-let [resolved (when (namespace name)\n    73\t                            (module/resolve-module\n    74\t                              registry\n    75\t                              (symbol (str (namespace name)\n    76\t                                           \".\"\n    77\t                                           (clojure.core/name name)))))]\n    78\t          resolved\n    79\t          (fail (str \"Unable to resolve symbol: \" name \" in this context\")\n    80\t                {:symbol name}))))))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn check-store-key!\n    84\t  \"Refuse a program store access whose key is a reserved name (Rule R):\n    85\t   the definition operator is never a store key.\"\n    86\t  [key]\n    87\t  (when (vm/reserved-name? key)\n    88\t    (vm/refuse-reserved! :store-key key)))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn store-put\n    92\t  \"The one program store write: every definition transition, the\n    93\t   `:vm/store-put` effect, and the four direct store instructions write\n    94\t   through here, and a reserved key is refused. Every other store write\n    95\t   `yin.vm.store-write-audit-test` detects is state construction on its\n    96\t   allowlist; that namespace states what it detects and the residual it\n    97\t   leaves to review.\"\n    98\t  [store key val]\n    99\t  (check-store-key! key)\n   100\t  (assoc store key val))\n   155\t## Development Workflow\n   156\t\n   157\t- Do not invent abstractions that hide streams.\n   158\t- Do not suggest mainstream frameworks unless explicitly asked.\n   159\t- Do not optimize prematurely.\n   160\t- When uncertain, ask at the architectural level, not the implementation level.\n   161\t- Explanations should align with Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp lineage.\n   162\t- Program store writes go through `engine/store-put`; any other store write\n   163\t  the store-write audit (`test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj`)\n   164\t  detects must be on its allowlist; its docstring states the residual it\n   165\t  leaves to review.\n   166\t\n   167\t### Problem Decomposition\n   168\t\n   169\tIf a problem appears complex:\n5\t1\ttest/yin/vm/semantic_engine_test.cljc\n5\t1\ttest/yin/vm/semantic_ffi_test.cljc\n14\t4\ttest/yin/vm/semantic_stream_observer_test.cljc\n30\t19\ttest/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc\n8\t5\ttest/yin/vm/telemetry_test.cljc\n15\t2\ttest/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc\n20\t15\ttest/yin/vm/ucf_test.cljc\n15\t8\ttest/yin/vm_test.cljc\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
