{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/rule_r_test.cljc | sed -n '1,135p;440,570p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '712,740p;783,815p;935,954p;975,990p;1196,1218p;1274,1288p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc | sed -n '355,405p;435,465p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc | sed -n '115,138p;500,520p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.rule-r-test\n     2\t  \"Rule R: `yin/def` is syntax, never a name. A variable naming it is\n     3\t   legal only as the operator of a two-operand definition whose first\n     4\t   operand is a literal symbol other than itself; it is never a binder, a\n     5\t   store key, a definition key, a macro name, or a primitive. Every\n     6\t   executing lookup refuses it (`engine/resolve-var`), every definition\n     7\t   transition writes its literal key without resolving its operator, and\n     8\t   every persistent-code loader requires and compares a contract stamp.\n     9\t\n    10\t   Each role is exercised on every loader (walker datoms and rows, semantic\n    11\t   datoms and vectors, stack, register), at transition time on raw walker\n    12\t   control, and at construction; the four backends agree on the stores a\n    13\t   definition program writes.\"\n    14\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    15\t            [dao.space.query :as query]\n    16\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    17\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    18\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n    19\t            [yin.vm.code :as code]\n    20\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-linearize :as dl]\n    21\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile :as rc]\n    22\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    23\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    24\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    25\t            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n    26\t            [yin.vm.macro :as m]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    28\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n    29\t            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t;; =============================================================================\n    33\t;; Helpers\n    34\t;; =============================================================================\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn- lit\n    37\t  [x]\n    38\t  {:type :literal, :value x})\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defn- v\n    42\t  [s]\n    43\t  {:type :variable, :name s})\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn- app\n    47\t  [f & args]\n    48\t  {:type :application, :operator f, :operands (vec args)})\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t(defn- lam\n    52\t  [params body]\n    53\t  {:type :lambda, :params params, :body body})\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(defn- def!\n    57\t  [k val]\n    58\t  (app (v 'yin/def) (lit k) val))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn- then\n    62\t  \"`first` for its effect, then `second`: `((fn [_] second) first)`.\"\n    63\t  [first-ast second-ast]\n    64\t  (app (lam '[_] second-ast) first-ast))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn- refusal\n    68\t  \"The ex-data of what `thunk` throws, unwrapping a loader's `:defect`, or\n    69\t   nil when it returns.\"\n    70\t  [thunk]\n    71\t  (try (thunk)\n    72\t       nil\n    73\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n    74\t         (let [d (ex-data e)]\n    75\t           (or (:defect d) d {})))))\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn- rule-of\n    79\t  [thunk]\n    80\t  (:rule (refusal thunk)))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn- segment-batch\n    84\t  \"A `:yin.code/*` segment batch whose instructions are `tuples`, positional\n    85\t   operands named by `code/vector-operand-table` (no `:pc` operands).\"\n    86\t  [tuples]\n    87\t  (into [[-1 :yin.code/type :segment 0 0]\n    88\t         [-1 :yin.code/length (count tuples) 0 0]]\n    89\t        (mapcat (fn [pc t]\n    90\t                  (let [e (- -2 pc)]\n    91\t                    (into [[e :yin.code/segment -1 0 0]\n    92\t                           [e :yin.code/pc pc 0 0]\n    93\t                           [e :yin.code/op (nth t 0) 0 0]]\n    94\t                          (map (fn [[attr _] x] [e attr x 0 0])\n    95\t                               (get code/vector-operand-table (nth t 0))\n    96\t                               (rest t)))))\n    97\t                (range)\n    98\t                tuples)))\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\t(defn- register-image\n   102\t  [n instructions]\n   103\t  {:bodies [{:locals 0, :registers n, :start 0,\n   104\t             :end (dec (count instructions))}],\n   105\t   :instructions instructions})\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- walker-run\n   109\t  [ast]\n   110\t  (vm/eval (tu/create-vm) ast))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(defn- semantic-run\n   114\t  [ast]\n   115\t  (vm/run (semantic/vm-load-program\n   116\t            (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream})\n   117\t            (linearize/lower-ast ast)\n   118\t            vm/semantic-contract)))\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\t(defn- stack-run\n   122\t  [ast]\n   123\t  (vm/run (dvm/create-vm (:image (dl/adapt (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n   124\t                         {:primitives vm/primitives,\n   125\t                          :make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   126\t                          :contract vm/stack-contract})))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t(defn- register-run\n   130\t  [ast]\n   131\t  (vm/run (rvm/create-vm (:image (rc/adapt (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n   132\t                         {:primitives vm/primitives,\n   133\t                          :make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   134\t                          :contract vm/register-contract})))\n   135\t\n   440\t      (let [tree (m/ast->packet (app (v 'yin/def) (lit 'yin/def) (lit 1)))\n   441\t            batch [:yin.program/batch [tree] 0 []\n   442\t                   [[:yin.macro/harvest 0 0 []]]]]\n   443\t        (is (= :definition-key\n   444\t               (:role (refusal #(m/expand-batch\n   445\t                                  batch (m/make-ctx {:token \"t\"}))))))))\n   446\t    (testing \"the transformer runner loads under the verified stamp\"\n   447\t      (is (= (m/ast->packet (lit 1))\n   448\t             (m/invoke macro [(m/ast->packet (lit 1))]\n   449\t                       (m/make-ctx {:token \"t\"})))))))\n   450\t\n   451\t\n   452\t(deftest a-macro-packet-runs-only-under-its-verified-stamp\n   453\t  (let [packet (m/ast->packet (lam '[x] (v 'x)))\n   454\t        operand (m/ast->packet (lit 1))\n   455\t        call-batch [:yin.program/batch [(m/ast->packet (app (v 'm) (lit 1)))]\n   456\t                    0 [] []]\n   457\t        cases {\"unstamped\" [packet :contract-missing],\n   458\t               \"old-stamped\" [(m/macro-entry packet \"v2\") :contract-mismatch],\n   459\t               \"a stamp but no contract\" [(m/macro-entry packet nil)\n   460\t                                          :contract-missing]}]\n   461\t    (doseq [[label [entry rule]] cases]\n   462\t      (testing label\n   463\t        (is (= rule (rule-of #(m/make-ctx {:token \"t\", :store {'m entry}})))\n   464\t            \"a seeded store is verified at context construction\")\n   465\t        (let [ctx (assoc (m/make-ctx {:token \"t\"}) :store {'m entry})]\n   466\t          (is (= rule (rule-of #(m/expand-batch call-batch ctx)))\n   467\t              \"a store supplied past make-ctx is verified by expand-batch\"))\n   468\t        (let [ctx (m/make-ctx {:token \"t\"})]\n   469\t          (is (= rule (rule-of #(m/invoke entry [operand] ctx)))\n   470\t              \"direct invoke verifies before it runs anything\"))))\n   471\t    (testing \"the runner itself loads only under the stamp it is handed\"\n   472\t      (let [req {:macro-tree packet, :env {'x operand},\n   473\t                 :prelude (m/prelude identity), :max-steps 1000}]\n   474\t        (is (= :contract-missing\n   475\t               (rule-of #(m/bounded-row-evaluator req))))\n   476\t        (is (= :contract-mismatch\n   477\t               (rule-of #(m/bounded-row-evaluator\n   478\t                           (assoc req :contract \"v2\")))))\n   479\t        (is (= {:value operand}\n   480\t               (m/bounded-row-evaluator\n   481\t                 (assoc req :contract vm/ast-contract))))))\n   482\t    (testing \"a current-stamped packet expands and runs\"\n   483\t      (let [entry (m/macro-entry packet vm/ast-contract)\n   484\t            ctx (m/make-ctx {:token \"t\", :store {'m entry}})]\n   485\t        (is (= :ok (:status (m/expand-batch call-batch ctx))))\n   486\t        (is (= operand (m/invoke entry [operand] ctx)))))\n   487\t    (testing \"a harvested macro is stamped by the expander that produced it\"\n   488\t      (let [tree (m/ast->packet (app (v 'yin/def) (lit 'm)\n   489\t                                     (lam '[x] (v 'x))))\n   490\t            batch [:yin.program/batch [tree] 0\n   491\t                   [[:yin.macro/definition 0 []]]\n   492\t                   [[:yin.macro/harvest 0 0 []]]]\n   493\t            r (m/expand-batch batch (m/make-ctx {:token \"t\"}))]\n   494\t        (is (= vm/ast-contract\n   495\t               (:yin.macro/contract (get-in r [:ctx :store 'm]))))))))\n   496\t\n   497\t\n   498\t;; =============================================================================\n   499\t;; Contract stamps\n   500\t;; =============================================================================\n   501\t\n   502\t(deftest every-persistent-code-loader-requires-and-compares-a-stamp\n   503\t  (let [ast (app (v '+) (lit 1) (lit 2))\n   504\t        datoms (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n   505\t        rows (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n   506\t        batch (linearize/lower-ast ast)\n   507\t        v1 (:vector (linearize/lower-rows rows))\n   508\t        stack-image (:image (dl/adapt datoms))\n   509\t        register-image* (:image (rc/adapt datoms))\n   510\t        loaders\n   511\t        {\"walker datoms\" [#(ast-walker/vm-load-program (tu/create-vm)\n   512\t                                                       datoms %)\n   513\t                          \"v2\"],\n   514\t         \"walker rows\" [#(ast-walker/vm-load-rows (tu/create-vm) rows %)\n   515\t                        \"v2\"],\n   516\t         \"semantic datoms\" [#(semantic/vm-load-program (semantic/create-vm)\n   517\t                                                       batch %)\n   518\t                            \"v2\"],\n   519\t         \"semantic vector\" [#(semantic/load-vector (semantic/create-vm) v1 %)\n   520\t                            \"v2\"],\n   521\t         \"stack\" [#(dvm/create-vm stack-image\n   522\t                                  {:primitives vm/primitives, :contract %})\n   523\t                  \"b1\"],\n   524\t         \"register\" [#(rvm/create-vm register-image*\n   525\t                                     {:primitives vm/primitives,\n   526\t                                      :contract %})\n   527\t                     \"r1\"]}]\n   528\t    (doseq [[label [load old]] loaders]\n   529\t      (testing label\n   530\t        (is (= :contract-missing (rule-of #(load nil)))\n   531\t            \"an unstamped load is refused\")\n   532\t        (let [d (refusal #(load old))]\n   533\t          (is (= :contract-mismatch (:rule d))\n   534\t              \"an old-stamped image with no definition fails by stamp\")\n   535\t          (is (= old (:actual d))))))\n   536\t    (is (= [vm/ast-contract vm/semantic-contract vm/stack-contract\n   537\t            vm/register-contract]\n   538\t           [\"v3\" \"v3\" \"b2\" \"r2\"]))\n   539\t    (testing \"vm/eval supplies the current stamp itself\"\n   540\t      (is (= 3 (vm/value (vm/eval (tu/create-vm) ast)))))))\n   541\t\n   542\t\n   543\t(deftest the-lowering-adapters-verify-the-incoming-stamp\n   544\t  (testing \"an adapter lowers only AST code whose own stamp it verified;\n   545\t            it never assigns one on the caller's behalf\"\n   546\t    (let [ast (app (v '+) (lit 1) (lit 2))\n   547\t          datoms (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n   548\t          rows (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n   549\t          load-ast (linearize/ast-loader semantic/vm-load-program)\n   550\t          load-rows (linearize/rows-loader semantic/load-vector)\n   551\t          adapters {\"ast-loader\" #(load-ast (semantic/create-vm) datoms %)\n   552\t                    \"rows-loader\" #(load-rows (semantic/create-vm) rows %)}]\n   553\t      (doseq [[label load] adapters]\n   554\t        (testing label\n   555\t          (is (= :contract-missing (rule-of #(load nil)))\n   556\t              \"an unstamped input is refused before lowering\")\n   557\t          (let [d (refusal #(load \"v2\"))]\n   558\t            (is (= :contract-mismatch (:rule d))\n   559\t                \"an old-stamped input is refused before lowering\")\n   560\t            (is (= \"v2\" (:actual d))))\n   561\t          (is (= 3 (vm/value (vm/run (load vm/ast-contract))))\n   562\t              \"a current-stamped input lowers, loads, and runs\")))))\n   563\t  (testing \"the explicitly trusted fresh-producer path supplies the stamp\"\n   564\t    (let [load (vm/fresh-code-loader\n   565\t                 (linearize/ast-loader semantic/vm-load-program)\n   566\t                 vm/ast-contract)]\n   567\t      (is (= 3 (vm/value (vm/run (load (semantic/create-vm)\n   568\t                                       (vm/ast->datoms\n   569\t                                         (app (v '+) (lit 1) (lit 2)))))))))))\n   570\t\n   712\t(defn bounded-row-evaluator\n   713\t  \"The default body runner (§5.2): a fresh throwaway ast-walker loaded from\n   714\t   the lambda body's rows, its parameters bound in `env`, the closed\n   715\t   `prelude` as its only primitives, no store, no module resolver, no stream\n   716\t   constructor, and no F