                          :type :dao.stream.apply/eval-operand}\n   437\t                         (:value state))))\n   438\t        :vm/gensym (let [prefix (or (:prefix node) \"id\")\n   439\t                         [id s'] (engine/gensym state prefix)]\n   440\t                     (assoc s'\n   441\t                            :value id\n   442\t                            :control nil\n   443\t                            :halted? (nil? k)))\n   444\t        :vm/store-get (do (engine/check-store-key! (:key node))\n   445\t                          (cesk-return state nil env k (get store (:key node))))\n   446\t        :vm/store-put (let [key (:key node)\n   447\t                            value (:val node)\n   448\t                            new-store (engine/store-put store key value)]\n   449\t                        (assoc state\n   450\t                               :store new-store\n   451\t                               :value value\n   452\t                               :control nil\n   453\t                               :halted? (and (not (:blocked? state)) (nil? k))))\n   454\t        :vm/store-update (let [key (:key node)\n   455\t                               f (:fn node)\n   456\t                               args (:args node)\n   457\t                               _ (engine/check-store-key! key)\n   458\t                               current (get store key)\n   459\t                               new-value (apply f current args)\n   460\t                               new-store (engine/store-put store key\n   461\t                                                           new-value)]\n   462\t                           (assoc state\n   463\t                                  :store new-store\n   464\t                                  :value new-value\n   465\t                                  :control nil\n   115\t   is empty. The store, the parked map, the wait set, the ready queue,\n   116\t   the id counter, and the composition values survive, exactly as they\n   117\t   survive a `yin.vm.semantic/load-vector`. A continuation parked under an\n   118\t   earlier image cannot be restored against this one: `stack-restore`\n   119\t   refuses it by H.\n   120\t\n   121\t   `contract` is required and compared with `vm/stack-contract` first\n   122\t   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`); the image must then pass\n   123\t   `yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect`, Rule R included. An empty segment\n   124\t   admits no code and needs neither.\"\n   125\t  [vm segment contract]\n   126\t  (when (seq segment)\n   127\t    (vm/check-contract! vm/stack-contract contract)\n   128\t    (when-let [defect (dcode/image-defect segment)]\n   129\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"Invalid stack image: \" (:rule defect))\n   130\t                      defect))))\n   131\t  (install-image vm segment))\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn create-vm\n   135\t  \"Build a fresh `DebruijnVM` over `segment` (a vector of instructions).\n   136\t\n   137\t   Options: `:free-env`, `:store`, `:primitives`, `:modules` (all default to\n   138\t   `{}`, matching the named VM's empty defaults except that `:primitives`\n   500\t        (assoc vm :pc (inc pc) :stack (conj stack (get store key))))\n   501\t\n   502\t      :store-put\n   503\t      (let [key (nth inst 1), value (nth inst 2)]\n   504\t        (assoc vm\n   505\t               :pc (inc pc)\n   506\t               :stack (conj stack value)\n   507\t               :store (engine/store-put store key value)))\n   508\t\n   509\t      ;; :define -- the definition transition: pop the value, write it\n   510\t      ;; under the literal name, and leave it as the expression's value.\n   511\t      ;; The operator is never resolved (Rule R).\n   512\t      :define\n   513\t      (let [value (peek stack)]\n   514\t        (assoc vm\n   515\t               :pc (inc pc)\n   516\t               :stack (conj (pop stack) value)\n   517\t               :store (engine/store-put store (nth in